{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: Sequence homology based on transcriptome-assembled sequence and known AMPs in databases. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (70.59%) to Cl-CATH2 R:21%; G:18%; L=F: 12%. GRAVY: -0.28; M Wt: 3975.762; Mol formula: C182H298N62O38; molar extinction coeff: 0. Activity: it exhibited antimicrobial activity against E. coli MTCC 739 (MIC 90 ug/ml), S. aureus MTCC 737 (MIC 75 ug/ml), and B. cereus clinical isolate (MIC 100 ug/ml). In vitro Toxicity: caused hemolysis of 2% human RBC (1 h incubation). Structure: it is helical in 50% TFE (CD). Updated 10/2023 after final publication.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "37907616", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Sci Rep. 2023 Oct 31;13(1):18728. doi: 10.1038/s41598-023-45875-w. Pub-Med.", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03617", "source_id": "AP03617", "source_numeric_id": "03617", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03617", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Transcriptome analysis of Corvus splendens reveals a repertoire of antimicrobial peptides.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
